docs {
  # Clinical Co-Pilot API collection

  Run the folders in order. Synthetic demo data only.

  1. Pick an environment (`local` or `deployed`).
  2. Fill in `client_secret` for the environment you picked (Configure > the environment > client_secret). The
     `client_id` is already set for `deployed`; for `local` it is whatever your own registration returned.
  3. Get an OpenEMR access token: Collection settings > Auth > OAuth 2.0 > Get Access Token. Sign in as the demo
     physician (credentials are provided with the submission). Copy the access token into the `access_token`
     environment secret.

     The requested scopes are `user/` only, deliberately - no `launch/patient`. A launch context binds the token to
     one patient on OpenEMR's side, and every session in this collection would then answer about that patient
     whatever `patient_id` it was given. Without it, the agent takes the patient from the request body and checks it
     against its own EVAL_PATIENT_IDS allowlist (ARCHITECTURE section 2).
  4. Run "0 Service", then each patient folder. Each folder opens its own session; the session handle is stored
     automatically and sent as `Authorization: Bearer` on the following requests.

  Every request has tests. Every response carries `X-Correlation-ID`, which matches the Langfuse trace and the audit table.
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: {{oauth_callback_url}}
  authorization_url: {{openemr}}/oauth2/default/authorize
  access_token_url: {{openemr}}/oauth2/default/token
  client_id: {{client_id}}
  client_secret: {{client_secret}}
  scope: {{scope}}
  pkce: true
}
